atrix\"><tbody>\n<tr><td>{{field-1}}</td></tr>\n<tr><td>{{field-2}}</td></tr>\n<tr><td>{{field-3}}</td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</div>\n</div>" :question/worked-solution "Differentiate each component twice, keeping the original component order.\n\nFor $x(t)=- 3 \\sqrt{t}$. Rewrite $- 3 \\sqrt{t}=-3t^{1/2}$ and apply the power rule twice.\n\nAfter the second power rule, $\\frac{3}{4}t^{-3/2}=\\frac{3}{4 t^{\\frac{3}{2}}}$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx'(t)&=- \\frac{3}{2 \\sqrt{t}} \\\\ x''(t)&=\\frac{3}{4 t^{\\frac{3}{2}}}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $y(t)=t^{3}$. Apply the power rule at both stages.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny'(t)&=3 t^{2} \\\\ y''(t)&=6 t.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $z(t)=- e^{2 - 3 t}$. Use the same inner argument at both stages; each differentiation contributes a factor of $-3$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nz'(t)&=3 e^{2 - 3 t} \\\\ z''(t)&=- 9 e^{2 - 3 t}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nReassemble the components:\n\n$$\n\\mathbf r''(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{3}{4 t^{\\frac{3}{2}}} \\\\ 6 t \\\\ - 9 e^{2 - 3 t}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186708141 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5daff037-b445-57fc-ad34-ae3fb96654ee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4 e^{2 t - 1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708126}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5daff037-b445-57fc-ad34-ae3fb96654ee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4 e^{2 t - 1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708126} :answer-field/id #uuid "46e6f5be-245f-5a23-a65e-e60eca33cfe1" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708123} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7dab690d-817f-5afa-a9dc-0501b37df8dc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{1}{t^{\\frac{3}{2}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708131}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7dab690d-817f-5afa-a9dc-0501b37df8dc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{1}{t^{\\frac{3}{2}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708131} :answer-field/id #uuid "c12f2a45-ebd7-5db4-b85b-08a01718c21c" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708142} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5921dacb-4228-5e58-ba90-3d74d0c8b1da" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 18 t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708125}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5921dacb-4228-5e58-ba90-3d74d0c8b1da" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 18 t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708125} :answer-field/id #uuid "e5bd6099-4cae-5588-9162-2a5cc8315f19" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708145}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "bf727b19-b774-5f43-9172-2c4d8af0f7b8" :question/problem "Given that\n\n$$\n\\mathbf r(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}e^{2 t - 1} \\\\ - 3 t^{3} \\\\ 4 \\sqrt{t}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nFind $\\mathbf r^{\\prime\\prime}(t)$ for $t>0$.\n\nEnter the components in their original order.\n\n<div class=\"matrix-answer\">\n<span class=\"matrix-answer-label\">$\\mathbf r''(t)=$</span>\n<div class=\"matrix-answer-brackets\">\n<table aria-label=\"Answer matrix\"><tbody>\n<tr><td>{{field-1}}</td></tr>\n<tr><td>{{field-2}}</td></tr>\n<tr><td>{{field-3}}</td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</div>\n</div>" :question/worked-solution "Differentiate each component twice, keeping the original component order.\n\nFor $x(t)=e^{2 t - 1}$. Use the same inner argument at both stages; each differentiation contributes a factor of $2$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx'(t)&=2 e^{2 t - 1} \\\\ x''(t)&=4 e^{2 t - 1}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $y(t)=- 3 t^{3}$. Apply the power rule at both stages.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny'(t)&=- 9 t^{2} \\\\ y''(t)&=- 18 t.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $z(t)=4 \\sqrt{t}$. Rewrite $4 \\sqrt{t}=4t^{1/2}$ and apply the power rule twice.\n\nAfter the second power rule, $-1t^{-3/2}=- \\frac{1}{t^{\\frac{3}{2}}}$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nz'(t)&=\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{t}} \\\\ z''(t)&=- \\frac{1}{t^{\\frac{3}{2}}}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nReassemble the components:\n\n$$\n\\mathbf r''(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}4 e^{2 t - 1} \\\\ - 18 t \\\\ - \\frac{1}{t^{\\frac{3}{2}}}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186708146 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a0a00c21-47eb-5e03-aa37-699633965c21" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{1}{2 t^{\\frac{3}{2}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708140}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a0a00c21-47eb-5e03-aa37-699633965c21" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{1}{2 t^{\\frac{3}{2}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708140} :answer-field/id #uuid "104a4d65-8fcb-5efe-b639-32cc72630618" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708113} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7fbc8cfc-6620-532f-9666-8284e7b8724a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 9 e^{- 3 t - 1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708132}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7fbc8cfc-6620-532f-9666-8284e7b8724a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 9 e^{- 3 t - 1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708132} :answer-field/id #uuid "1b064683-e04b-5825-9cd7-4c6ebb7cddc5" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708115} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3c9f66df-47e3-59e2-8c9b-29f5c5ec0976" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 36 t^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708120}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3c9f66df-47e3-59e2-8c9b-29f5c5ec0976" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 36 t^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708120} :answer-field/id #uuid "98118b13-b501-5672-ab45-53f2cbe4ed36" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708139}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "eb373ab6-81fa-5d8b-a86f-9f919eb63526" :question/problem "Given that\n\n$$\n\\mathbf r(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}- e^{- 3 t - 1} \\\\ 2 \\sqrt{t} \\\\ - 3 t^{4}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nFind $\\mathbf r^{\\prime\\prime}(t)$ for $t>0$.\n\nEnter the components in their original order.\n\n<div class=\"matrix-answer\">\n<span class=\"matrix-answer-label\">$\\mathbf r''(t)=$</span>\n<div class=\"matrix-answer-brackets\">\n<table aria-label=\"Answer matrix\"><tbody>\n<tr><td>{{field-1}}</td></tr>\n<tr><td>{{field-2}}</td></tr>\n<tr><td>{{field-3}}</td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</div>\n</div>" :question/worked-solution "Differentiate each component twice, keeping the original component order.\n\nFor $x(t)=- e^{- 3 t - 1}$. Use the same inner argument at both stages; each differentiation contributes a factor of $-3$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx'(t)&=3 e^{- 3 t - 1} \\\\ x''(t)&=- 9 e^{- 3 t - 1}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $y(t)=2 \\sqrt{t}$. Rewrite $2 \\sqrt{t}=2t^{1/2}$ and apply the power rule twice.\n\nAfter the second power rule, $- \\frac{1}{2}t^{-3/2}=- \\frac{1}{2 t^{\\frac{3}{2}}}$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny'(t)&=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{t}} \\\\ y''(t)&=- \\frac{1}{2 t^{\\frac{3}{2}}}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $z(t)=- 3 t^{4}$. Apply the power rule at both stages.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nz'(t)&=- 12 t^{3} \\\\ z''(t)&=- 36 t^{2}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nReassemble the components:\n\n$$\n\\mathbf r''(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}- 9 e^{- 3 t - 1} \\\\ - \\frac{1}{2 t^{\\frac{3}{2}}} \\\\ - 36 t^{2}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186708151 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "441b0873-3bd6-5c6d-87ce-68aac5aa22d5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\langle 36 t^{2},\\,20 t^{3}\\right\\rangle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708155} {:answer/id #uuid "776bdf86-915d-5ee2-b638-046bbde959d9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\langle 3 t^{4},\\,20 t^{3}\\right\\rangle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708161} {:answer/id #uuid "8ae68666-53ea-5314-86af-068e867a307a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\langle 36 t^{2},\\,t^{5} - 2 t\\right\\rangle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708163} {:answer/id #uuid "ca4406d1-6bee-58ce-81ad-3d9b3a8c8396" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\langle - 36 t^{2},\\,20 t^{4}\\right\\rangle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708170} {:answer/id #uuid "ceea0309-2157-5d7f-96d2-660f3ebaf478" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\langle 3 t^{4},\\,t^{5} - 2 t\\right\\rangle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708171}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "441b0873-3bd6-5c6d-87ce-68aac5aa22d5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\langle 36 t^{2},\\,20 t^{3}\\right\\rangle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708155} :answer-field/id #uuid "9fea8edc-7266-5942-a60d-982ecc684bd2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708165}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1ec36838-342e-5c18-8f2e-0448afa34ade" :question/problem "Given that\n\n$$\n\\mathbf r(t)=\\left\\langle 3 t^{4},\\,t^{5} - 2 t\\right\\rangle.\n$$\n\nFind $\\mathbf r^{\\prime\\prime}(t)$." :question/worked-solution "Differentiate each component twice, keeping the original component order.\n\nFor $x(t)=3 t^{4}$. Apply the power rule at both stages.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx'(t)&=12 t^{3} \\\\ x''(t)&=36 t^{2}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $y(t)=t^{5} - 2 t$. Apply the power rule at both stages. A linear term has zero second derivative.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny'(t)&=5 t^{4} - 2 \\\\ y''(t)&=20 t^{3}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nReassemble the components:\n\n$$\n\\mathbf r''(t)=\\left\\langle 36 t^{2},\\,20 t^{3}\\right\\rangle.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186708152 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4354310e-3d3d-5a7f-88b4-14768baf10aa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\langle - 40 t^{4},\\,9 t^{2}\\right\\rangle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708154} {:answer/id #uuid "aaaca2a5-1e3d-5ad2-ae54-76fe1422eb16" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\langle - 2 t^{5},\\,3 t^{3}\\right\\rangle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708166} {:answer/id #uuid "b421d516-93ec-52df-9a42-49f490360e7a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\langle - 40 t^{3},\\,18 t\\right\\rangle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708167} {:answer/id #uuid "baef2185-3ae4-53e0-8cde-1de3c97ce582" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\langle - 40 t^{3},\\,9 t^{2}\\right\\rangle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708168} {:answer/id #uuid "e1019a93-06a4-5805-bc6b-53bcf5ede57b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\langle - 40 t^{4},\\,18 t\\right\\rangle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708174}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b421d516-93ec-52df-9a42-49f490360e7a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\langle - 40 t^{3},\\,18 t\\right\\rangle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708167} :answer-field/id #uuid "334392ec-dde1-53b4-a020-65fa983aea5d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708153}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "20a10e89-815a-53f1-8c2d-e16a6be250c3" :question/problem "Given that\n\n$$\n\\mathbf r(t)=\\left\\langle - 2 t^{5},\\,3 t^{3}\\right\\rangle.\n$$\n\nFind $\\mathbf r^{\\prime\\prime}(t)$." :question/worked-solution "Differentiate each component twice, keeping the original component order.\n\nFor $x(t)=- 2 t^{5}$. Apply the power rule at both stages.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx'(t)&=- 10 t^{4} \\\\ x''(t)&=- 40 t^{3}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $y(t)=3 t^{3}$. Apply the power rule at both stages.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny'(t)&=9 t^{2} \\\\ y''(t)&=18 t.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nReassemble the components:\n\n$$\n\\mathbf r''(t)=\\left\\langle - 40 t^{3},\\,18 t\\right\\rangle.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186708164 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "13930583-fbc7-545c-92b4-867745b97aaf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\langle - 12 t^{2},\\,- 20 t^{3}\\right\\rangle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708150} {:answer/id #uuid "62bbdd23-ef27-52b8-ae76-ce15653279cb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\langle - t^{4} - 2 t,\\,- t^{5} - t\\right\\rangle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708158} {:answer/id #uuid "83ec97be-f885-5f06-a83d-ec4d0c8333a6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\langle - t^{4} - 2 t,\\,- 20 t^{3}\\right\\rangle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708162} {:answer/id #uuid "c2037bf4-efd7-516a-a0f0-dbf3f7ae7c57" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\langle - t^{4} - 2 t,\\,- 5 t^{3}\\right\\rangle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708169} {:answer/id #uuid "d003093a-2ed0-50a0-aaa0-29cb768dfd60" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\langle - 12 t^{2},\\,- t^{5} - t\\right\\rangle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708172}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "13930583-fbc7-545c-92b4-867745b97aaf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\langle - 12 t^{2},\\,- 20 t^{3}\\right\\rangle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708150} :answer-field/id #uuid "087109de-afc0-560e-adb3-df03cdceea23" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708149}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9f655fcb-be66-5209-94a0-95a54f9c3246" :question/problem "Given that\n\n$$\n\\mathbf r(t)=\\left\\langle - t^{4} - 2 t,\\,- t^{5} - t\\right\\rangle.\n$$\n\nFind $\\mathbf r^{\\prime\\prime}(t)$." :question/worked-solution "Differentiate each component twice, keeping the original component order.\n\nFor $x(t)=- t^{4} - 2 t$. Apply the power rule at both stages. A linear term has zero second derivative.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx'(t)&=- 4 t^{3} - 2 \\\\ x''(t)&=- 12 t^{2}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $y(t)=- t^{5} - t$. Apply the power rule at both stages. A linear term has zero second derivative.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny'(t)&=- 5 t^{4} - 1 \\\\ y''(t)&=- 20 t^{3}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nReassemble the components:\n\n$$\n\\mathbf r''(t)=\\left\\langle - 12 t^{2},\\,- 20 t^{3}\\right\\rangle.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186708176 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4ca2670f-b145-5b51-bf1f-00d363fcbe93" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\langle 18 t,\\,12 t\\right\\rangle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708156} {:answer/id #uuid "6221122c-0587-5731-960f-a382458bf93b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\langle - 18 t,\\,12 t\\right\\rangle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708157} {:answer/id #uuid "63fd5e0e-3792-595b-b1c7-e3b555e44943" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\langle 18 t,\\,- 12 t\\right\\rangle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708159} {:answer/id #uuid "713c8194-ad9b-5163-8d43-cb4ce3eaa537" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\langle - 18 t,\\,- 12 t\\right\\rangle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708160} {:answer/id #uuid "e4b9ec8e-d62e-596c-8df5-f858bf01a09a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\langle - 9 t^{2} - 1,\\,- 2 t^{3}\\right\\rangle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708175}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "713c8194-ad9b-5163-8d43-cb4ce3eaa537" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\langle - 18 t,\\,- 12 t\\right\\rangle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708160} :answer-field/id #uuid "d52df412-2944-5b2b-8aee-6ce2ab05da77" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708173}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e5d053bc-3af0-5ff7-8c9a-8ab9cf7b6d39" :question/problem "Given that\n\n$$\n\\mathbf r(t)=\\left\\langle - 3 t^{3} - t,\\,- 2 t^{3}\\right\\rangle.\n$$\n\nFind $\\mathbf r^{\\prime\\prime}(t)$." :question/worked-solution "Differentiate each component twice, keeping the original component order.\n\nFor $x(t)=- 3 t^{3} - t$. Apply the power rule at both stages. A linear term has zero second derivative.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx'(t)&=- 9 t^{2} - 1 \\\\ x''(t)&=- 18 t.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $y(t)=- 2 t^{3}$. Apply the power rule at both stages.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny'(t)&=- 6 t^{2} \\\\ y''(t)&=- 12 t.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nReassemble the components:\n\n$$\n\\mathbf r''(t)=\\left\\langle - 18 t,\\,- 12 t\\right\\rangle.\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "The Second Derivative of a Vector-Valued Function"}]}
